Z||000000||speed racer||07-22-2000||11:46 PM||||The clips on my 86 sun roof are lose is their any why to tighten them?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||07-23-2000||10:46 PM||||If you mean they are loose on the glass you should be able to simply tighten the screws/nuts.  If you mean that they are loose in the mounting holes in the roof panel when the glass is installed then you probably need new clips. (I'm assuming that you are talking about the metal tabs that slip into the roof when you install the glass panel).<P>My roof rattled when I got it and it leaked a bit.  I got new clips and hardware from the Pontiac dealer for about $15.00 and it sure tightened everything up.  The plastic coating had worn off of the clips and allowed them to rattle.  The new screws came with an integral washer that sealed to the glass.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
